reconcile.overall:
The final REPORT.md keeps the right central verdict: keep PPO, fix the construction for signal, smoothness and hardware reasons, and run canonical training as the structural fix. It also carries every item from check.json (R0-R14). The reviser never saw the critiques or draft 1, though, and about two dozen substantive points from them were dropped or silently contradicted.

Five places where the report contradicts itself or its own sources:
- **Seeds.** §6.2 says to screen on seeds {1,2,3} and, in the same line, "never use the incumbent's s2/s3" (REPORT:285).
- **Missing control.** §5.2 requires "no reproduction by an action_rate-only control", but no such arm is budgeted. The INC0 arm was dropped.
- **C_40 branch.** It drops side speed as a gate on a FAST C_40_s2 result. CHARTER P10 reads FAST-late as "(ii) contributes", and FAST-on-schedule is already excluded by the 0.180 early read.
- **Unmeasurable kill read.** C_lr_bound's RSI-start kill read cannot be measured, because C_lr runs with RSI off (candidates_v15.yaml:366).
- **Rung 3 bed.** Rung 3 is budgeted as 3,000-iteration arms from scratch, yet the report itself says the throttle binds only late. Draft 1 and the critiques put it on a conditional tail fork.

Four statements in the body that the evidence contradicts:
- **M1's turn-facing z.** It is −2.020, not −2.07; 2.073 is the R value (MQ CHANGELOG.md:20).
- **W's logged action_rate.** It is 0.275 per max-episode-second, because Isaac Lab divides Episode_Reward by max_episode_length_s (reward_manager.py:120). That is ≈0.34 per alive-second, so the R2 "correction" is backwards.
- **"Two independent Monte Carlos".** The two sets of increments in §4.3 come from the same simulation measured against different baselines. The skeptic's genuinely independent run was dropped.
- **Hardware runtime "not checked".** The critiques did check it: there is no clamp in the runtime mapper (compute/parkour/mappers/model_to_hardware.py:92-100), and the sent command is fed back as the previous action (inference_client.py:278).

Two implementation hazards were dropped, and both can make arm A silently inert or its σ check pass vacuously:
- ActorCriticRMA keeps unknown policy kwargs without checking them (actor_critic_with_encoder.py:142). I verified this.
- A soft-σ parameter makes the runner log Policy/mean_noise_std as 0.0 (runner :545-551).

Dropped algorithm-family content:
- the conditional TD3-lean path, which is the most direct answer to "is PPO the barrier?";
- the family-swap condition that wall-clock or sample count must be shown to be binding;
- REPPO and the fallback head;
- the FPO++ reassessment and the warning against pip-installing RSL-RL-SAC.

Smaller drops:
- kill reads and the slope rule;
- the pooled-R definition for 3-5 seeds;
- the survival tripwire margin: 0.2 has a ~21 % false-trip rate at 3v3;
- the rollout-length ramp hazard and the env-count re-baselining in rung 4;
- the telemetry details: KL under every schedule, the D7 minibatch-0 KL and the namespace;
- the DAgger LR coupling;
- the confirm-cost fork and the P1_canon alternative;
- the B<k> rerun cost for s3+s2;
- deploy details: student estimator mismatch, stale compute copy, canonical head undeployable;
- the rule to distil bounded teachers on clip(μ);
- the caveat that the literature rests on single preprints.

The §10 check log is mostly consistent with the body. Its stale or wrong entries are:
- R0 ("write blocked"), which is stale;
- R1 (z value);
- R2 (0.275/s, and the "both Monte Carlos" claim);
- R10 ("not checked").

The header's "critiques not kept as files" is also wrong: they are in artifacts/decision/challenge_*.json. Each issue below gives restore-or-defend guidance and exact wording.

issues.issue:
The deploy-contract defect is only partly carried over, and the report says "I did not check whether the hardware runtime clamps downstream" when the critiques did check it: it does not. Four points were dropped:
(a) the runtime mapper has no clip and feeds the sent (raw) command back as previous_action, which reproduces the PR #2019 loop at deploy;
(b) the deploy (student) exporter substitutes the estimator, but student training and every student eval do not, which also corrects dossier C16 (DOS :805);
(c) the compute/parkour module copy is stale and cannot build CrabHexActorCriticRMA;
(d) a canonical-training head cannot be distilled or deployed without runtime or student support.
With the bound loss chosen over tanh, the export clamp becomes mandatory; a bound loss does not remove the clip dependency.

Several early kill reads for rung 2 were dropped, and the only kill point left is iteration 1000. Missing:
- the DEAD read (track_ratio_mean < 0.40 at iteration 1000);
- the σ-collapse read (σ < 0.1 at iteration 1000);
- an inert-knob read at iteration 200-300 (|μ| > 1 share still > 0.8 means the knob did nothing);
- the slope rule (an arm that is behind but has a steeper final-500 slope is not killed).
The inert-knob read matters because X6's silent-kwarg and σ-tag hazards would otherwise surface only after ≈0.4 GPU-h per arm, and only if the σ tag is right.

"Win at the pooled R" is undefined for 3-5 seeds. The driver's pooled R is max(R_eval/√2, R_seed): it averages two seeds and never shrinks the seed term. The report's √3 MDEs (±0.084) therefore do not match the decision statistic. The design critique's analysis rules were dropped:
- judge by a pre-registered script using cell means, pooled within-cell SD with its t df, and a permutation null;
- run arms as driver references;
- a process-floor pair before the screen;
- randomised run order;
- the Q-block threshold.

Several load-bearing telemetry details were dropped:
- KL computed under every schedule (it is adaptive-only today);
- the minibatch-0 KL, which measures the UNRESOLVED dossier D7 term for free;
- the pre-clip gradient norm and the share of minibatches above max_grad_norm (the surrogate alone gives 17.7-22.7 against a clip of 1.0);
- explained variance computed before in-place advantage normalisation;
- RNG-free logging under a PPO/ namespace with no 'symmetry' or 'mirror' in tag names, because run_phases' mirror-active check is a regex on those words.
§4.2 also dropped the DAgger coupling: hist_encoder_optimizer is built at the same configured LR, so any LR arm also moves the history-encoder LR.

